from pathlib import Path
import pandas as pd,numpy as np,json
B=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];R=B/'results'
a=pd.read_csv(R/'shortlist_evaluation.csv');lp=pd.read_csv(R/'continuous_worst_regret.csv');st=pd.read_csv(R/'all630_rank_acceptability.csv');short=pd.read_csv(R/'shortlists_evidence.csv');mc=pd.read_csv(R/'mc_error_summary.csv');pair=pd.read_csv(R/'paired_regret_differences.csv');ov=pd.read_csv(R/'shortlist_overlap.csv');pre=pd.read_csv(R/'greedy_prefix_evaluation.csv');ties=pd.read_csv(R/'tie_diagnostics.csv')
con=json.loads((R/'CONCLUSIONS.json').read_text());metric=json.loads((R/'metric_audit.json').read_text())
main=['historical10','AV10','AHV10','robust10'];core=a[(a.split.isin(['test','replication']))&a['set'].isin(main)]
full=core[core.space=='full'];fulltest=full[full.split=='test'].set_index('set');rob=short[short['set']=='robust10'];ss=st[(st.split=='test')&(st.space=='full')].set_index('pair')
summary={'freeze_commit':'cff3e81eebf93a16df6da8a21fe735c1554a5a8f','metric_audit':metric,'conclusions':con,'same_k_test_and_replication':core.to_dict('records'),'continuous_worst_regret':lp.to_dict('records'),'robust10_evidence':rob.to_dict('records'),'overlap':ov.to_dict('records'),'monte_carlo_error':mc.to_dict('records'),'paired_differences':pair[pair.split!='train'].to_dict('records'),'full_test_mean_regret_reduction_fraction':1-fulltest.loc['robust10','regret_mean']/fulltest.loc['historical10','regret_mean'],'full_continuous_worst_regret_reduction_fraction':1-lp[(lp.space=='full')&(lp['set']=='robust10')].continuous_worst_regret.iloc[0]/lp[(lp.space=='full')&(lp['set']=='historical10')].continuous_worst_regret.iloc[0],'known_failures':['Three robust10 candidates lack archived rule-level HB review.','No improvement over historical10 in ordered/local spaces; all have continuous regret zero.','AHV full front has 41 candidates and zero regret; cardinality differs from k10.','The greedy10 full-space regret remains positive; it is not an optimality result.','Observed ranks/acceptability are distribution dependent; no architect preferences sampled.']}
# JSON NaN is not interoperable; convert through pandas JSON for evidence records.
summary['robust10_evidence']=json.loads(rob.to_json(orient='records'))
(R/'SUMMARY.json').write_text(json.dumps(summary,indent=2,allow_nan=False)+'\n')
lines=['# Preference-robust screening: complete results and limitations','','## Frozen design','Protocol was committed before new outcomes at cff3e81eebf93a16df6da8a21fe735c1554a5a8f. The analysis uses 20,000 independent samples for each of three spaces and each of train, test, replication (180,000 total), plus a resolution-100 grid and candidate-wise LP audit of each fixed set. Greedy selection uses only 60,000 equally pooled training samples. All 630 candidates remain in ranking analysis.','','## Primary result',f"On full-simplex independent test weights, mean regret fell from {fulltest.loc['historical10','regret_mean']:.9f} to {fulltest.loc['robust10','regret_mean']:.9f}; p95 fell from {fulltest.loc['historical10','regret_p95']:.9f} to {fulltest.loc['robust10','regret_p95']:.9f}. Winner coverage rose from {fulltest.loc['historical10','winner_coverage']:.5%} to {fulltest.loc['robust10','winner_coverage']:.5%}.",'The restricted ordered and local spaces yield zero regret for every same-k method, including the historical shortlist. Therefore the benefit is protection against broad preference uncertainty, especially extreme intervention-cost preferences, rather than universal improvement. The preregistered stable-improvement rule is met because full-space mean and p95 improve in both independent runs while restricted spaces are equal. This is not an empirical claim about architects.',f"A/H correlations: Pearson {metric['pearson_A_H']:.9f}, Spearman {metric['spearman_A_H']:.9f}. N is exactly zero for all 630. A measures area crossing the low-sun threshold, while H measures mean direct-sun duration gain; correlated but not equivalent outcomes.",'','## Independent test and replication, equal k=10','|Space|Split|Set|Mean regret|p95 regret|Observed max|Winner coverage|Any Top10 coverage|','|---|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for r in core.itertuples():lines.append(f'|{r.space}|{r.split}|{r.set}|{r.regret_mean:.9f}|{r.regret_p95:.9f}|{r.regret_max:.9f}|{r.winner_coverage:.5f}|{r.any_top10_coverage:.5f}|')
lines+=['','## Continuous worst-case audit','All 630 candidate-wise LPs per fixed set/space passed. The maximum is global over the declared continuous polyhedral preference space, up to numerical solver tolerance; it is not a certificate that the selected set is optimal.','|Space|Set|Size|Continuous worst regret|Witness wA,wH,wV|','|---|---|---:|---:|---|']
for r in lp.itertuples():lines.append(f'|{r.space}|{r.set}|{len(short[short["set"]==r.set])}|{r.continuous_worst_regret:.9f}|{r.wA:.6f}, {r.wH:.6f}, {r.wV:.6f}|')
lines+=['','## Robust10, greedy insertion order','Five entries overlap the historical10; Jaccard = 1/3. A/V front has 12 entries; A/H/V front has 41. Neither front required padding in its Top10 comparator. Full-front comparisons have different cardinalities and are diagnostics only.','|Step|Pair|Historical rank|A m2|H h|V m3|Full test Top10 acceptability|HB cohort|Translation|','|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---|']
for r in rob.itertuples():lines.append(f'|{r.position}|{r.pair}|{r.historical_rank}|{r.A:.3f}|{r.H:.9f}|{r.V:.3f}|{ss.loc[r.pair,"top10_acceptability"]:.5f}|{r.HB_cohort}|{r.design_translation_status}|')
lines+=['','## Monte Carlo precision','All candidate-specific winner/Top10 Wilson intervals are retained in all630_rank_acceptability.csv; these are marginal conditional Monte Carlo intervals, not architect-preference probabilities or simultaneous uncertainty bounds. Test and replication are separate draws and never affect selection. Pooled mean standard errors use the stratified equal-space design; within-space coverage intervals use Wilson.','|Space|Metric|Median absolute test/replication difference|p95 difference|Maximum difference|','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|']
for r in mc.itertuples():lines.append(f'|{r.space}|{r.metric}|{r.median_absolute_delta:.6f}|{r.p95_absolute_delta:.6f}|{r.max_absolute_delta:.6f}|')
lines+=['','## Interpretation and failure cases','- The full A/H/V front attains zero continuous regret because positive-weight linear winners have nondominated representatives; that requires 41 candidates here. The 10-item greedy set still has positive full-space regret.','- The A/V front can miss H-driven winners. Truncating either front by historical score is an explicit baseline, not a claim that Pareto filtering naturally supplies a unique best Top10.','- C12,C15; C15,C25; and C24,C35 lack archived rule-level HB results. Missing high-fidelity evidence must remain visible; do not describe all ten as validated. Existing HB evidence comes from the curated23 or frozen20 cohorts; no cohort was reselected.','- N=0 is a property of this archived pure-height-reduction universe, not a guarantee for later translated designs.','- Weights are declared scenarios. Uniform-simplex sampling is a modeling assumption, not preference-free or a population survey. The local half-width 0.10 and ordered constraints are assumptions.','- Normalization is frozen from this candidate universe. Correlation of A and H and redundancy deserve discussion; no learned or elicited weights were fitted.','- Worst observed rank differs from worst possible rank. Exact utility ties use stable natural numeric pair order; tie diagnostics are archived. Utility winner coverage is separately reported to avoid confusing rank-ID ties with utility loss.','- The run is archived-performance decision analysis only. No new Honeybee/Radiance, structural, rights, cost, or construction validation was run.','- Findings demonstrate one-site implementation and preference sensitivity. They do not establish novelty of SMAA, minimax regret, utility elicitation or Pareto theory.','','## Reproduction','Run python icores_2027/preference_robust/analysis/run_analysis.py from the repository, then python icores_2027/preference_robust/analysis/make_report.py. See RUN_MANIFEST.json and requirements.txt for versions. The run verifies frozen input hashes before generating any weights. No network, GPU, or geometry simulator is required.','The initial run needed reporting-only corrections: stratified pooled MC SE, explicit HiGHS version, and local rejection acceptance count. Initial affected artifacts are retained under audit/initial_reporting_run. Rerun uses identical frozen seeds and rules; shortlist and outcomes are unchanged.']
(B/'RESULTS_AND_LIMITATIONS.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
print('Report and SUMMARY.json written')
